course: dictionary
lesson: 7302
title: Many meanings of pitch
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning the author means. The word pitch is a good example: it can mean a sports field, how high or low a sound is, or putting up a tent.
explain: «Walk a little way into a cave and the daylight disappears; deeper in, it is pitch black all day and all year.» Daylight disappearing and all year tell you that pitch black means completely dark. It is not a sound or a sport here.
explain: «Many small insect-eating bats shout high-pitched calls and listen to the echoes.» The word high-pitched describes the calls, so pitch means how high or low a sound is. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then test it in the sentence.
explain: «3 rugby union matches played at the same time: 3 × 30 = 90 players on the pitches.» Matches and players show that a pitch is a field for a sport. Try each meaning, and keep the one that makes sense.
fact: Pitch has several meanings, so check the context before you choose one.
fact: A pitch can be a sports field, especially in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: Pitch can also mean how high or low a sound is: faster vibrations make a higher pitch.
fact: «Pitch black» means completely dark, as in a cave with no daylight.
fact: To pitch a tent means to put it up; in baseball, to pitch means to throw the ball.
exercise: «Walk a little way into a cave and the daylight disappears; deeper in, it is pitch black all day and all year.» What does pitch black mean? | Very high and loud | Wet and muddy | *Completely dark | A sports field at night
exercise: «Many small insect-eating bats shout high-pitched calls and listen to the echoes.» What does pitch tell you about the calls? | How far they can throw | Whether they are made of tar | *How high or low the sound is | Which sports field they were on
exercise: «3 rugby union matches played at the same time: 3 × 30 = 90 players on the pitches.» What is a pitch in this sentence? | A tent put up for camping | *A field for playing a sport | A high sound | A black sticky substance
test: Mum says, «Let's pitch the tent before dark.» What does pitch mean? | *To put up | To fall forward | To shout very high | To throw a ball
test: Dan sings a note with a low pitch. What does pitch mean here? | Completely dark | *How low a sound is | A sports field | To throw a ball
exam: In «Anyone on the pitch can score, defend or save the game», what is the pitch? | A talk to persuade people | A black sticky tar | A high sound | *A sports field
